    "name": "Salience Network Gating of DMN/TPN Switching",
    "description": "The anterior insula and dACC act as a gatekeeper switch between the Default Mode Network (DMN) and Task Positive Network (TPN). The switch is triggered when aggregate salience (sensory, interoceptive, threat) exceeds a dynamic threshold. Soft fascination and restoration occur when the environment provides enough stimulation to sustain interest but keeps aggregate salience below the switching threshold.",
